{% include "fact-extraction-instructions.jinja2" %}
{% if audience_summary %}
Extract only what the supplied audience perspective supports. Preserve the complete attribution, uncertainty, established belief, tense, time and qualifications in each fact's text. A report is a report, not an observation or a world-truth update. Do not infer acceptance or invent events. The host assigns the source audience; do not include a known_by field. Only reference supplied prior fact IDs, and do not supersede an observation merely because someone reports a conflicting claim.
Each fact may include "time_scope": an exact explicit ISO date or timestamp appearing in BOTH its text and the source, or null when the source does not anchor the fact to an explicit time. Do not convert relative dates, invent a date or use acquisition time as event time.{% if not facts_only %} Preserve this phrase in the summary too.{% endif %} With no supported facts return [].
Each fact must include "evidence_id": the ID of ONE offered evidence span below that supports its entire statement, including attribution and uncertainty, or null if no single offered span supports it. Never invent an ID, infer a private fact from a public span, or cite a span merely because it mentions the same person or topic. A fact with null evidence stays within its extraction audience. The same evidence may support multiple distinct facts. Continue extracting supported facts from the audience prose even when the evidence list is empty.
Offered evidence IDs with short excerpts (fully perceived by this audience; use the audience prose above for the complete statement):
{{ fact_evidence | default('') }}
{% endif %}
<FACTS>
<a JSON list of the atomic facts established in {{ summary_target }}. One object per fact: {"text": "one self-contained statement, names spelled out, no pronouns", "importance": 2, "subjects": ["names of the characters, items or places the fact is about"], {% if line_ids %}"message_id": "the bracketed id of the line that establishes the fact, copied exactly", {% endif %}{% if audience_summary %}"evidence_id": "one offered evidence ID, or null", "time_scope": "exact date or timestamp copied from BOTH source and fact text, or null if unanchored",{% else %}"known_by": ["characters who learned this fact during {{ summary_target }}"], "restates": "id of a known fact this statement repeats without adding anything, or null",{% endif %} "supersedes": "id of a known fact this one replaces, or null"}. Choose importance 1, 2, or 3 using the rules above.{% if line_ids %} Every fact must carry the message_id of the one line that establishes it; a fact without a valid line id is discarded.{% endif %} {% if audience_summary %}Use supersedes only for a fact that changes or replaces an earlier one.{% else %}A restatement is recorded against the known fact, not as a new one: use restates for an unchanged repeat and supersedes only for a fact that changes or replaces an earlier one.{% endif %} Facts only: events that happened, decisions taken, things revealed, states that changed. Between 0 and 12 items. Output the JSON list and nothing else between the tags.>
</FACTS>
